\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((2x-3y)+(2{x}_{\\text{new}}-3{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-3y)-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-3y)-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-y)-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-y) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{5}(2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(1)$ and $y(2).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+1=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{5}(2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(2\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =0.20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=1,\\,y=0.20.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{5}(2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2-0.20) \\\\  & =\\frac{29}{25} \\\\  & =1.16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ny(1)≈0.20,\\,y(2)≈1.16.\n$$" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327196 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327197 13194139535020 true] [17592186327196 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327198 13194139535020 true] [17592186327196 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327199 13194139535020 true] [17592186327196 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535020 true] [17592186327196 1041 "field-1" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327196 1104 #edb/ref