6327204 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535020 true] [17592186327204 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-x+5y,\\,y(-1)=2\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with two steps to approximate $y(0)$ and $y(1),$ rounded to two decimal places.\n\n$$\ny(0)≈{{field-1}},\\,y(1)≈{{field-2}}\n$$" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327204 1113 #uuid "06e11280-02d9-55eb-ba08-45ad211f8038" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327204 1145 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(-1)$ and asked to find $y(1).$ The distance from $x=-1$ to $x=1$ is $2,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-(-1)}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((-x+5y)+(-{x}_{\\text{new}}+5{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+5y)+\\frac{5}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+5y)+\\frac{5}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+7y)+\\frac{5}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+7y) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{3}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}-7y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(0)$ and $y(1).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=-1,\\,y=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=-1+1=0.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{3}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}-7y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(-1+0-7\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+1=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{3}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}-7y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(0+1-7\\cdot (-5)) \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ny(0)≈-5.00,\\,y(1)≈12.00.\n$$" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327206 13194139535020 true] [17592186327205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327207 13194139535020 true] [17592186327205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327208 13194139535020 true] [17592186327205 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535020 true] [17592186327205 1041 "field-1" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327205 1104 #edb/ref 17592186327208 13194139535020 true] [17592186327205 1110 #uuid "2b3117ce-e931-5e73-b7ba-2a07e3e9a6e4" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327206 1034 "-4.81" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327206 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535020 true] [17592186327206 1111 #uuid "3440780b-e39d-50dc-ad6c-552ae9d4490c" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327207 1034 "-3.00" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327207 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535020 true] [17592186327207 1111 #uuid "9726ad27-aefb-5b9f-8792-6e0978fe521a" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327208 1034 "-5.00" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327208 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535020 true] [17592186327208 1111 #uuid "20949bf0-84c0-5987-8c09-d494adc2012b" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327210 13194139535020 true] [17592186327209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327211 13194139535020 true] [17592186327209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327212 13194139535020 true] [17592186327209 1040 #e