solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{8}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{8}(-3x-3{x}_{\\text{new}}+9y) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{7}(-3x-3{x}_{\\text{new}}+9y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(\\frac{1}{4})$ and $y(\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{7}(-3x-3{x}_{\\text{new}}+9y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}(-3\\cdot 0-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+9\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4} \\\\  & =3.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{4},\\,y=3.75.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{7}(-3x-3{x}_{\\text{new}}+9y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}(-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+9\\cdot (3.75)) \\\\  & =4.50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ny(\\frac{1}{4})≈3.75,\\,y(\\frac{1}{2})≈4.50.\n$$" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327223 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327224 13194139535020 true] [17592186327223 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327225 13194139535020 true] [17592186327223 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327226 13194139535020 true] [17592186327223 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535020 true] [17592186327223 1041 "field-1" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327223 1104 #edb/ref 17592186327226 13194139535020 true] [17592186327223 1110 #uuid "80a75f88-1730-549e-82a7-e65fb82e77a6" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327224 1034 "3.21" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327224 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535020 true] [17592186327224 1111 #uuid "d9923254-46db-5e7e-a783-29f6bdb9e6ab" 13194139535020 true] [17592186327225 1034 "2.89" 13194139535020 true] [1